{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":261103,"duration_api_ms":322091,"num_turns":47,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"e39914b7-5418-43bb-80be-daecdb6108ef","total_cost_usd":2.31206545,"usage":{"input_tokens":35,"cache_creation_input_tokens":86586,"cache_read_input_tokens":2438592,"output_tokens":7247,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":86586,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":35,"outputTokens":7247,"cacheReadInputTokens":2438592,"cacheCreationInputTokens":86586,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.9418085000000005,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":1819,"outputTokens":11021,"cacheReadInputTokens":1735142,"cacheCreationInputTokens":111855,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.3702569499999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Reviewed all key implementation files for the B7 bead (snapshot/API chemistry semantics, display conversions, and TDS/conductivity labeling). The implementation is well-structured and addresses the acceptance criteria comprehensively:\n\n1. **Conversion constants centralized** in `conversions.rs` with correct molar mass ratios; round-trip tests verify accuracy within 1e-12 tolerance.\n2. **Snapshot field renames** use explicit unit suffixes (`_mg_n_per_l`, `_mg_p_per_l`, `_mg_c_per_l`, `estimated_tds_7_ion_mg_per_l`, `estimated_conductivity_us_cm`), making units unambiguous.\n3. **Legacy backward compatibility** is robust: custom `Deserialize` impl normalizes old field names to canonical ones with canonical precedence; API responses emit both old and new names plus metadata.\n4. **TDS/conductivity** correctly labeled as estimates with documented 7-ion scope and omitted-contributor lists propagated to TUI and API.\n5. **Concentration helpers** centralized on `WaterState` and `ConcentrationView`, replacing scattered inline division.\n6. **GH/KH formulas** refactored from magic numbers (2.497, 4.118) to named molar-mass-ratio constants — computed values match.\n7. All 25+ relevant tests pass (conversion round-trips, snapshot serialization/deserialization, legacy alias handling, TUI label assertions, API response enrichment).\n\nFound two items worth flagging as amendments.","amendments":[{"body":"The `conversions.rs` module (NO3_PER_N, NO2_PER_N, NH4_PER_N, NH3_PER_N, PO4_PER_P and all 10 forward/inverse conversion functions) is entirely unused outside its own test module. No production code, TUI, or API path imports or calls any of these constants or functions. While the acceptance criteria call for centralized conversion logic and the module is well-tested internally, it is dead code. Either (a) wire at least one display path (e.g. the TUI chemistry screen or the API `chemistry_field_semantics` response) to actually use these conversions for an optional ion-basis display column, so the module has a live consumer, or (b) gate the module behind a `#[cfg(test)]` or explicitly document it as preparatory infrastructure so clippy dead-code warnings won't fire and future maintainers don't remove it.","rationale":"Dead code that satisfies an acceptance criterion on paper but has no runtime consumer is fragile — it can drift from the actual display path without anyone noticing because no integration test exercises the full element→ion→display pipeline."},{"body":"The new `co2_aq_mmol_per_l` field on `TankSnapshot` (and its deserialization proxy `TankSnapshotRepr`) is required with no `#[serde(default)]` annotation and has no entry in `LEGACY_SNAPSHOT_CHEMISTRY_FIELD_ALIASES`. Any external consumer that has cached or stored a snapshot JSON from a previous version (before this field existed) will fail to deserialize it with a missing-field error. Add `#[serde(default)]` on the `co2_aq_mmol_per_l` field in `TankSnapshotRepr`, or add it as a legacy alias mapping to itself, so old snapshot payloads without this field still parse (defaulting to 0.0).","rationale":"The save system uses TankState (not TankSnapshot) so save files are unaffected, but the TUI API client deserializes `/snapshot` responses into `TankSnapshot`. During a rolling upgrade where the API server is updated before the TUI client (or vice versa), or if snapshot JSON is cached/logged externally, the missing required field will cause a hard deserialization failure."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"b5876397-2401-4225-a7fa-920144cc21ad"}
